1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,510
The first arc closed, not with a victory, but with a bridge.

2
00:00:04,510 --> 00:00:16,563
By the end of the term, the map had grown into three small tools: a printed page, a phone page, and a person who answered questions at the gate.

3
00:00:16,563 --> 00:00:25,516
Such work was largely invisible, and the university and the union mentioned it once and twice, respectively.

4
00:00:25,516 --> 00:00:33,690
The president of the university wrote one line about it; the young leader of the union wrote four.

5
00:00:33,690 --> 00:00:37,344
The existing system did not change.

6
00:00:37,344 --> 00:00:45,208
A student stood at the same locked door; a boy from the college office still had to phone his supervisor.

7
00:00:45,208 --> 00:00:52,171
What had changed was the likelihood of being seen, and that change was only partly visible.

8
00:00:52,171 --> 00:00:59,220
A single angry message could disrupt the whole week, so they answered every one the same day.

9
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:03,210
“We manage a small thing,” Maya said.

10
00:01:03,210 --> 00:01:13,238
“That is all.” Her tone was expressive rather than triumphant, and she had begun to develop a thicker skin about it.

11
00:01:13,238 --> 00:01:19,217
The peak of the year came on a gorgeous evening in the living room of the volunteer house.

12
00:01:19,217 --> 00:01:26,931
The metro had brought them a box of aging posters and a bag of trash; the lighting was terribly bad.

13
00:01:26,931 --> 00:01:36,189
Aerial photographs of the campus lay beside a scenic sketch of the river, and the argument that followed erupted like a volcano.

14
00:01:36,189 --> 00:01:46,122
The lead volunteer read a personal note from the head of her major, and the mood turned riotous, then thunderous, then quiet.

15
00:01:46,122 --> 00:01:50,806
Their produce for the term fitted in one folder.

16
00:01:50,806 --> 00:01:55,581
The disruption was partly internal and partially financial.

17
00:01:55,581 --> 00:02:00,355
The resultant delay saddened Lin and made Maya resent the meeting.

18
00:02:00,355 --> 00:02:06,474
“It is pointless to build an evolutionary plan and then starve it,” she said.

19
00:02:06,474 --> 00:02:17,956
“A plan has to nourish the people in it.” The attainment they wanted, namely a permanent sign, now depended on a budget they did not control.

20
00:02:17,956 --> 00:02:26,760
“This is the most populous district in the city,” she added, “and we cannot even repair one frame.”

21
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:35,943
A shameless poster about “super students” hung beside the library, and a voluminous folder of outdated rules sat beneath it.

22
00:02:35,943 --> 00:02:40,907
The blossoms in the square had opened and the daylight lasted longer.

23
00:02:40,907 --> 00:02:46,826
“Every volunteer had to contribute one page,” Professor Zhao said.

24
00:02:46,826 --> 00:03:15,906
“Our work is disruptive in a very small way, and that is exceedingly fruitful.” A phrasal verb in her notebook, she admitted, was only partly relevant, but the sentence she copied beside it was this: “A bridge is not a victory, and without it there is no crossing.” A first map does not teach you a city; it teaches you how many doors you have not tried.
